Patch-Id: ASTRA-0017
Title: Paint the Astra ground instead of the Firefox pre-XUL silhouette
Tier: P2
Upstream-Files: mozglue/misc/PreXULSkeletonUI.cpp
Intent: Astra's first frame is its own dark ground; the Windows pre-XUL skeleton's Firefox toolbar/tab silhouettes are a false frame and its light theme flashes white before XUL. Flatten the skeleton to the product background while keeping the early window.
Risk: low (Windows-only pre-XUL paint, no Linux/macOS code path)
Test: forge lint, forge import --check; startup capture shows a solid Astra ground with no Firefox toolbar silhouette or white frame
Verified-On: 153.6.0
Removal-Plan: none anticipated; replace with an Astra-owned native splash if one is built
---
diff --git a/mozglue/misc/PreXULSkeletonUI.cpp b/mozglue/misc/PreXULSkeletonUI.cpp
index 2135283774..734ddf21f1 100644
--- a/mozglue/misc/PreXULSkeletonUI.cpp
+++ b/mozglue/misc/PreXULSkeletonUI.cpp
@@ -702,8 +702,25 @@ bool FillRectWithColor(HDC hdc, LPCRECT rect, uint32_t mozColor) {
 
 Result<Ok, PreXULSkeletonUIError> DrawSkeletonUI(
     HWND hWnd, CSSPixelSpan urlbarCSSSpan, CSSPixelSpan searchbarCSSSpan,
-    Vector<CSSPixelSpan>& springs, const ThemeColors& currentTheme,
+    Vector<CSSPixelSpan>& springs, const ThemeColors& currentThemeArg,
     const EnumSet<SkeletonUIFlag, uint32_t>& flags) {
+  // Astra paints its own chrome; the Firefox toolbar silhouette would be a
+  // false first frame. Keep the pre-XUL window as the product's dark ground
+  // until the app frame paints.
+  ThemeColors astraTheme = currentThemeArg;
+  astraTheme.backgroundColor = 0x1c1b22;
+  astraTheme.toolbarForegroundColor = astraTheme.backgroundColor;
+  astraTheme.titlebarColor = astraTheme.backgroundColor;
+  astraTheme.tabColor = astraTheme.backgroundColor;
+  astraTheme.tabOutlineColor = astraTheme.backgroundColor;
+  astraTheme.chromeContentDividerColor = astraTheme.backgroundColor;
+  astraTheme.urlbarColor = astraTheme.backgroundColor;
+  astraTheme.urlbarBorderColor = astraTheme.backgroundColor;
+  astraTheme.animationColor = astraTheme.backgroundColor;
+  const ThemeColors& currentTheme = astraTheme;
+  urlbarCSSSpan = {0, 0};
+  searchbarCSSSpan = {0, 0};
+  springs.clear();
   // NOTE: we opt here to paint a pixel buffer for the application chrome by
   // hand, without using native UI library methods. Why do we do this?
   //
